<bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
<head>Biographical Information
</head>
<p>John Brockwell, Jr., was born in Petersburg, Virginia, 27 October 1945 to John Brockwell (1890-1980) and Bessie Beach Brockwell (1893-1928).  John Brockwell, Jr., attended schools in Petersburg, graduating from Petersburg High School in 1942.  He worked for Brown and Williamson Tobacco Corporation before enlisting in the United States Army on 29 March 1943.  Brockwell served in the 194th Glider Infantry, 17th Airborne Division, receiving his training at Camp Lee in Virginia and Camp Mackall in North Carolina.  Brockwell was killed in action in France, 24 March 1945.  He was buried in Champigneul #1 Cemetery in Marne, France, after his death, and reinterred in Blandford Cemetery in Petersburg in December 1948.
</p>
<p>John Brockwell's Purple Heart and the flag from his military interment at Blandford Cemetery are located at the Virginia War Memorial.</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Papers, 1924-2008, of John Brockwell, Jr. (1924-1945), of Petersburg, Virginia, consisting of letters to his parents, and to his sister, Ruth Brockwell (1927-2020), while serving in 194th Glider Infantry, 17th Airborne Division in World War II.  Collection includes correspondence regarding Brockwell's death in action, as well as papers from his time as a student at Petersburg High School, photographs, and other documents regarding his military service.  Includes condolences from Secretary of War Henry Stimson (1867-1950) and General George C. Marshall (1880-1959), as well as certificates of honor from Presidents Lyndon B. Johnson and Jimmy Carter.
</p>
</scopecontent>
